  "title": "Up on the Housetop",
  "composer": "Benjamin Hanby",
  "about": "Benjamin Hanby wrote this Christmas song in 1864, while he ran a singing school in New Paris, Ohio. It was first published by Root & Cady in the magazine Our Song Birds. It is thought to be the first Christmas song mainly about Santa Claus. Hanby wrote some 80 songs before he died of tuberculosis in 1867.",
  "funFact": "One book counts it as the second-oldest Christmas song that is not religious. Only Jingle Bells, written in 1857, is older.",
